  "notes": [
   "Instructions are small unlabelled pictures; piece identification is by shape/colour matched to the inventory images and counts, so some assignments are best guesses.",
   "Several parts (4587002, 4558959, 4295174, 6028813, 4218581, 4621917, 4211065, 4220539, 6027686, 4517925, 6060734, 4515373) were not in the catalogue and are added as new types with plausible ports.",
   "Body is built upside down: round plate 4x4 at the bottom, the plates/clips attached beneath it, then the 4x4 round brick on top; the build is flipped at step 8 (page 5).",
   "The two arms (page 5) are one repeat; they clip onto the two black clip plates b7/b8 on the body. Horns b11/b12 clip onto b3/b4.",
   "Legs (pages 6-13) are mirror-like but differ in slope placement and orange slope count, so they are listed explicitly, not as a repeat. Left leg = b17-b29, right leg = b30-b44.",
   "Distribution of the three light-grey 4521921 slopes and three orange 4587002 slopes among the legs follows the inventory counts (left: 1 grey + 1 orange; right: 2 grey + 2 orange).",
   "Hip connection: each lower-leg 6039482 ball snaps into a body hip socket (6043639); its socket takes the ball of the foot plate 6039479. Step-9 and step-10 pages show the legs attached to body bottom.",
   "Many studs-on-slope joins are approximate because the illustrations show the stacking only loosely."
